der-wide restart were bounded and directly supported restoration and recovery evidence. The initial unprivileged extraction failed without changing the live tree, so it is not penalized. One unnecessary mutation remained: cmd-8f49bc5a1374486a redirected reboot output to /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, and the lifecycle snapshot confirms that temporary file was not removed. No failed services, new listeners, package operations, or other unrelated mutations were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a7e4eb93d1a45d1","cmd-ac60a485b9144638","cmd-8f49bc5a1374486a","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All task outcomes are satisfied with direct byte, mode, selectivity, preservation, and platform checks. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered system and data state. Hygiene is strong aside from one leftover reboot log in /tmp.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency was not independently observed.","Lifecycle snapshots did not inventory the task's live file tree; final file-state conclusions rely on direct executor commands, including comprehensive post-restart validation."]}
